{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Analyzer",
  "description": "Monitors source code files for changes and provides suggestions for code quality improvements, including identifying code smells, recommending design patterns, and highlighting best practices for better readability, maintainability, and performance.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "**/*.go",
      "**/*.ts",
      "**/*.tsx",
      "**/*.js",
      "**/*.jsx",
      "**/*.py",
      "**/*.java",
      "**/*.cpp",
      "**/*.c",
      "**/*.h",
      "**/*.cs",
      "**/*.rb",
      "**/*.php",
      "**/*.swift",
      "**/*.kt",
      "**/*.rs"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified code in the changed file for potential improvements. Focus on:\n\n1. **Code Smells**: Identify any code smells such as duplicated code, long methods, large classes, excessive parameters, or inappropriate intimacy between classes.\n\n2. **Design Patterns**: Suggest applicable design patterns that could improve the code structure and maintainability.\n\n3. **Best Practices**: Check for adherence to language-specific best practices, naming conventions, and coding standards.\n\n4. **Readability**: Evaluate code clarity, comment quality, and suggest improvements for better understanding.\n\n5. **Maintainability**: Identify areas that could be refactored for easier maintenance, testing, and extension.\n\n6. **Performance**: Spot potential performance issues like inefficient algorithms, unnecessary computations, or resource leaks.\n\n7. **Error Handling**: Review error handling patterns and suggest improvements for robustness.\n\n8. **Security**: Flag any obvious security concerns or vulnerabilities.\n\nProvide specific, actionable suggestions with code examples where appropriate. Maintain the existing functionality while proposing improvements. Prioritize the most impactful suggestions first."
  }
}